{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Go with the men, but only, etc.</b> It is possible that He said: \"Go with the men, but only the thing that I shall speak to you — that you shall speak,\" and you shall inform them of this. Or its meaning is that after he confessed, \"If it is evil in Your eyes I will turn back\" (Numbers 22:34), He said to him: Go with them, for I have forgiven your sin, provided only that you remember the warning with which I warned you. And it was necessary to say this to him, so that he not think that He told him \"go with them\" to do what they asked of you. It is also possible that the one going desired to curse the people and had no desire to bless them in any way, and therefore Elohim warned him at every time that he would speak with Him. And because of this, Balaam informed Balak at the beginning of his speaking with him: \"Behold, I have come to you\" (Numbers 22:38) — for in the coming alone I was permitted, but regarding the matter of the people, am I able to say anything according to your desire? The thing that Elohim puts in my mouth — that I shall speak, whether curse or blessing. See if you desire that I speak concerning them, and if you do not desire this, I will turn back from now on."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:57.507419652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}